    <string name="study_about_title">About</string>
    <string name="study_about_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="study_about_body">An educational, clean-room reconstruction of a weather app\'s architecture. It contains no Samsung code, artwork or strings, and it talks to no Samsung service.\n\nWeather data is provided by Open-Meteo.com under the CC BY 4.0 licence, through an in-process gateway that serves the project\'s own data shapes.</string>
    <string name="study_about_licences">Open source licences</string>
    <string name="study_licences_title">Open source licences</string>
    <string name="study_licences_body">Weather and geocoding data\nOpen-Meteo.com — CC BY 4.0. Geocoding data from GeoNames — CC BY 4.0.\n\nToolbar glyphs\nMaterial Symbols — Apache License 2.0.\n\nLibraries\nAndroidX (core, appcompat, fragment, recyclerview, viewpager2, constraintlayout, coordinatorlayout, swiperefreshlayout, navigation, lifecycle, room, work, datastore, startup, glance) — Apache License 2.0\nMaterial Components for Android — Apache License 2.0\nKotlin and kotlinx.coroutines — Apache License 2.0\nDagger and Hilt — Apache License 2.0\nRetrofit, OkHttp and Moshi — Apache License 2.0\nOrbit MVI — Apache License 2.0\nCoil — Apache License 2.0\nGoogle Play services location — Android Software Development Kit License\n\nThe weather icons and all other drawings in this app are original to this project.</string>
    <string name="study_activities_title">Activities</string>
    <string name="study_activities_body">Activity forecasts (running, golf, driving and the like) are a capability of specific weather providers. The provider in use does not supply them, so there is nothing to choose here.</string>
